endmodule

question_text:
Design a purely combinational module dut with the following interface:
- input [7:0] in
- input [2:0] ctrl
- output [7:0] out

You are provided a combinational submodule dut_dependency_2 with ports (in0, in1, sel, out) that behaves as a 2:1 multiplexer: out equals in1 when sel=1, otherwise in0. Your solution must be constructed exclusively from dut_dependency_2 instances and wires as specified below; no other logic is allowed.

Declare intermediate wires x[7:0] and y[7:0]. Build three cascaded mux stages controlled by ctrl[2], ctrl[1], and ctrl[0] respectively:

Stage A (compute x with ctrl[2]):
- x[7]=mux(in[7], 1’b0, ctrl[2]); x[6]=mux(in[6], 1’b0, ctrl[2]);
- x[5]=mux(in[5], 1’b0, ctrl[2]); x[4]=mux(in[4], 1’b0, ctrl[2]);
- x[3]=mux(in[3], in[7], ctrl[2]); x[2]=mux(in[2], in[6], ctrl[2]);
- x[1]=mux(in[1], in[5], ctrl[2]); x[0]=mux(in[0], in[4], ctrl[2]).

Stage B (compute y with ctrl[1]):
- y[7]=mux(x[7], 1’b0, ctrl[1]); y[6]=mux(x[6], 1’b0, ctrl[1]);
- y[4]=mux(x[4], x[6], ctrl[1]); y[3]=mux(x[3], x[5], ctrl[1]);
- y[2]=mux(x[2], x[4], ctrl[1]); y[1]=mux(x[1], x[3], ctrl[1]);
- y[0]=mux(x[0], x[2], ctrl[1]).
Additionally instantiate mux(x[5], x[7], ctrl[1]) with its output intentionally left unconnected; do not drive y[5].

Stage C (compute out with ctrl[0]):
- out[7]=mux(y[7], 1’b0, ctrl[0]); out[6]=mux(y[6], y[7], ctrl[0]);
- out[5]=mux(y[5], y[6], ctrl[0]); out[4]=mux(y[4], y[5], ctrl[0]);
- out[3]=mux(y[3], y[4], ctrl[0]); out[2]=mux(y[2], y[3], ctrl[0]);
- out[1]=mux(y[1], y[2], ctrl[0]); out[0]=mux(y[0], y[1], ctrl[0]).

Instantiate exactly these muxes with instance names ins_17..ins_10, ins_27..ins_20, and ins_07..ins_00 corresponding to Stages A, B, and C respectively. No clock/reset; outputs reflect inputs combinationally.

